<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	  Without this entitlement `registerForRemoteNotifications` fails at
	  runtime with "no valid aps-environment entitlement string found", and
	  the app never gets a token: `Info.plist` asking for the
	  remote-notification background mode is only half of it.

	  The value is a build setting rather than a literal because the two
	  environments are different servers at Apple, and a build signed for one
	  cannot receive pushes sent to the other. `APS_ENVIRONMENT` is
	  `development` for Debug and Profile and `production` for Release —
	  TestFlight builds are Release, and so use production APNs, which is what
	  the server's own `APNS_ENVIRONMENT` has to be set to as well.
	-->
	<key>aps-environment</key>
	<string>$(APS_ENVIRONMENT)</string>

	<!--
	  Universal Links are NOT configured here yet, on purpose.

	  `com.apple.developer.associated-domains` is a capability, not a plain
	  key: adding it here makes signing fail unless the App ID has Associated
	  Domains enabled and the provisioning profile was regenerated with it. CI
	  builds iOS with `--no-codesign` and would not catch that — the TestFlight
	  workflow would, by breaking.

	  There is also nothing to point it at: `privio.channel` is not registered,
	  so no `apple-app-site-association` would be fetched from it.

	  The order to do it in, when the domain exists, is in
	  `docs/invite-links.md`. Until then `privio://` in `Info.plist` is what
	  opens a link, and it needs none of this.
	-->
</dict>
</plist>
